 2.1Plant material, inoculation and infection validation
 The host was the fully susceptible A. thaliana line Col-eds1.2 wrr7 [23], which is highly susceptible to the oomycete A. candida (white blister rust) race 4 isolate AcEM2. Seeds were obtained from a certified stock centre. Five 6 × 4 cell trays were filled with a well-drained soil:sand substrate (F2s), and an additional pot with the same mix was used for germination. Seeds were broadcast, vernalised at 4 °C in darkness for 72 h, and transplanted at one plant per cell. Trays stood in water-filled catch trays to maintain uniform moisture by capillarity. Humidity lids were removed at the first true-leaf stage. Unless stated otherwise, conditions were 22 °C, 16 h light/8 h dark, ~60% relative humidity and 120–150 μmol m−2 s−1 photosynthetic photon flux density. Seedlings were inoculated about three weeks after transplanting, when rosettes bore four to five true leaves.
-Spray guns, flasks and bottles were wiped with 100% ethanol before use. Leaves bearing visible A. candida pustules were suspended in chilled sterile water, and sporangia were dislodged by gentle agitation, filtered through nylon mesh and diluted on ice to 105 spores ml−1. Controls received sterile water only. A single run used 96 seedlings (72 inoculated, 24 mock-inoculated). Both leaf surfaces were misted to run-off. Trays were then held at 4 °C for 24 h and placed in a cabinet at 22 °C with 10 h light and 18 °C with 14 h dark until 2 dpi, after which standard growth conditions resumed. Symptoms were assessed visually on the abaxial surface at each imaging time point [CONFIRM: whether the 7 and 10 dpi inspections in the earlier draft refer to later observations outside the 2, 4 and 6 dpi imaging schedule; sporulation is now reported from about 6–8 dpi]. To validate latent infection, trypan blue staining was performed at 2, 4 and 6 dpi on a reserved subset of leaves at each time point and examined microscopically as described previously [24]. [SUPERVISOR TO CONFIRM: number of leaves stained per treatment and time point, whether mock controls were stained, and the proportion showing positive staining.]
