 4.7Limitations
-This study has several limitations. (i) The data come from a single experimental run of 96 plants, with only 24 mock-inoculated plants, so estimates are imprecise (Table 11). Infected and mock-inoculated plants were also kept on separate trays, so treatment is confounded with tray position and local growth conditions, and the mock tray was always imaged before the infected tray, so treatment was consistently correlated with acquisition order. The lamp was left running after a 15 min warm-up and the camera geometry was not reset between trays, which lowers the chance of a tray-specific set-up difference, but drift within a session cannot be excluded. Plant-disjoint folds are not independent of batch, cultivation cycle, inoculum preparation, calibration session, illumination or operator; the results are not evidence of generalisation. (ii) The host was a single, highly susceptible mutant line and the pathogen a single isolate, so the effect sizes may not transfer to crops or to partially resistant genotypes. (iii) The same plants were imaged at each time point, so the tasks are not independent. (iv) Spectra were dark-corrected and wavelength-calibrated but not converted to reflectance, which limits comparison across sessions and the interpretation of spectral magnitudes. (v) Exposure was fixed at 2 s but analogue gain was automatic and not logged, the band–wavelength mapping must be restored, and instrument characteristics such as spectral resolution, signal-to-noise ratio and registration accuracy were not characterised (Table 2). The acquisition size (2592 × 1944 pixels) is below the native resolution of the sensor, and autofocus means focus was not identical across samples. (vi) No abiotic stresses were included, although drought and nutrient deficiency produce overlapping spectral responses [7,28]. (vii) Only one optical configuration and illumination geometry were evaluated, and infection was sampled at three discrete time points. (viii) Model timing was measured on a data-centre GPU only. (ix) Spectral statistics and model attribution are in progress.
